{# ------------------------------------------------------- no-downtime block #}
<section class="section section--pale" data-reveal>
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The bit everyone worries about</p>
      <h2>Nobody stops working because of us</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        A warehouse that stops moving is a warehouse losing money every hour.
        That is the first question we ask about, not the last.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <ul class="checks">
        <li><strong>Zone by zone.</strong> We work one section at a time so aisles stay open and stock stays reachable.</li>
        <li><strong>After hours and weekends.</strong> Nights, Sundays and public holidays, when the floor is empty.</li>
        <li><strong>Shutdown periods.</strong> We plan around your Christmas and summer shutdown so the work happens while you are already stopped.</li>
        <li><strong>Plant keeps running.</strong> We isolate and protect machinery, and we do not move stock for you without asking.</li>
        <li><strong>A written programme.</strong> You get the plan in writing before anyone starts — dates, zones, access, and what we need from you.</li>
        <li><strong>One point of contact.</strong> You get a name and a number, not a call centre.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/">Tell us your shutdown dates</a> and we will tell you honestly
        whether working in them is worth it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

